note irequiv fixture (issue 826): hex digit value, a real duplicate pair.
note js_hexv (seed/json/json.om line 582) and hhexv (seed/net/http.om line 332)
note are identical at omega-mv 62d1d0d6. Their ret ulong sub c K lines are each
note split into d = sub c K / ret ulong d here, because omc IR mode at that
note revision refuses a conversion of a computed operand (error 7, ir_cast).
note hexfold is a refactor: one letter range after or c 32 folds case.
note hexoff1 is a deliberate mutant (le c 70 became lt c 70): it differs
note from the others at exactly one input, c = 70 ('F').
fn js_hexv c uchar to ulong
if and ge c 48 le c 57
d = sub c 48
ret ulong d
end
if and ge c 97 le c 102
d = sub c 87
ret ulong d
end
if and ge c 65 le c 70
d = sub c 55
ret ulong d
end
ret 16
end
fn hhexv c uchar to ulong
if and ge c 48 le c 57
d = sub c 48
ret ulong d
end
if and ge c 97 le c 102
d = sub c 87
ret ulong d
end
if and ge c 65 le c 70
d = sub c 55
ret ulong d
end
ret 16
end
fn hexfold c uchar to ulong
if and ge c 48 le c 57
d = sub c 48
ret ulong d
end
l = or c 32
if and ge l 97 le l 102
d = sub l 87
ret ulong d
end
ret 16
end
fn hexoff1 c uchar to ulong
if and ge c 48 le c 57
d = sub c 48
ret ulong d
end
if and ge c 97 le c 102
d = sub c 87
ret ulong d
end
if and ge c 65 lt c 70
d = sub c 55
ret ulong d
end
ret 16
end
